From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kernel <noreply@localhost>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 00:47:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: camss: add SM6225 (khaje) support; dts node

S6b, the CAMSS core, going the upstream CAMSS route:

- New binding qcom,sm6225-camss modeled on qcm2290
  with the khaje counts (3x CSIPHY/CSID/VFE, no TPG -
  downstream TPG blocks have no IRQs and the driver
  has no TPG subdevs in this family).
- Driver: csiphy/csid/vfe resource tables cloned from
  the 2290 ones (CSIPHY 3ph-1.0, CSID-340, VFE-340)
  extended with the third unit, ICC table shared, and
  version kept at CAMSS_2290 so all code paths are the
  qcm2290 ones. Sub-IP register identity with 2290 is
  a downstream-data-based assumption (CSIPHY is
  'v1.2.1' downstream); not yet hardware-verified.
- SoC node camss@5c6e000 (disabled): 10 register
  windows / 9 IRQs / 20 clocks from the GCC CAMSS set
  (already defined in gcc-khaje), TOP GDSC, bengal
  interconnect paths (ahb/hf_mnoc/sf_mnoc) and the two
  downstream ISP IOMMU contexts (0x400, 0x800).
- Board wires the CSIPHY analog supplies
  (pm6125_l18 on the historical '1p2' name, pm6125_l4
  on '1p8' - downstream mipi-csi-vdd2/vdd1 resp.).
  Node stays disabled until the sensors land (S6c).
---
